                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I really, really want to reccommend this. I do. But there's just too many issues. \n\nPros\n\nA unique fighting experience that I've really enjoyed so far.\nInterestingly mapped out story mode. Looks to have a decently long story.\nI love the design in general. Of the game, and where the lore comes from as well. \n\nCons\n\nThe translation is god awful. It's really bad. There are some cutscenes where the text is in Chinese, when clearly english was chosen.\n\nThe game constantly flickers for me. It gives me errors about my graphics card, and as the game gets more intense, it becomes more impossible for me to play it. My setup is more than enough to run this game, so unless it's a compatability issue with nvidia gtx graphics (unlikely), I don't see the issue.\n\nVery, very little options as far as changing visual settings go. Literally all that's there is an option to change the resolution.\n\n\nI hope I can reccommend this game someday.\n\nIn case you're about to buy this, here's my rig :\n\nIntel Core i7 4720HQ (2.60 GHz) 8 GB Memory 1 TB HDD NVIDIA GeForce GTX 960M 2 GB GDDR5 15.6\" Windows 10 Home 64-Bit \n\nIf yours are like mine, I would NOT reccommend this game to you.\n\n\n\n",
